id #uuid "59ed1787-672a-57bb-b86d-43224b917d2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-34772" :question/problem "Let $B={{b}_{1},{b}_{2},{b}_{3}}$ be a basis of ${R}^{3}$ and $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C={{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}},$ where ${c}_{1}=3{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=-{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=4{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =-3{b}_{1}+4{b}_{2}-6{b}_{3} \\\\  & =4{b}_{2}-6{b}_{3}-3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}(3{b}_{2})+6(-{b}_{3})-\\frac{3}{4}(4{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{3}{c}_{1}+6{c}_{2}-\\frac{3}{4}{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{4}{3} \\\\ 6 \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186410061 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29b27833-e930-5339-89b3-c5651d791dcd" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Two-Dimensional Vector in a Different Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4acab282-04ec-5eb0-ae3a-7ab839526ee4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410024} {:answer/id #uuid "ad9fccc8-89c8-5084-95ed-898b492b9317" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410037} {:answer/id #uuid "af3b103c-e7ac-56f6-8025-6eee882f5637" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{3} \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186410038} {:answer/id #uuid "f26fb59e-92cb-5f2d-bb4b-31538da03416" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{a